course: dictionary
lesson: 5953
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the words around it show you which one is meant. «Matabele ants of Africa raid termites» uses Matabele for a kind of ant, not a group of people.
explain: «The Matabele live around Bulawayo in south-western Zimbabwe» uses the same word for a people. The place clues tell you so. Check by swapping in your meaning: ants do not live around a city, so the people meaning must fit here.
explain: History lessons about southern Africa and colonial wars also use this word. Today the people are usually called Ndebele, so you may read both names in different books.
fact: Matabele names a people of south-western Zimbabwe, around the city of Bulawayo.
fact: Matabeleland is the region where they live.
fact: Today the people are usually called Ndebele.
fact: The same word is also used for a kind of African ant, as in «Matabele ants of Africa raid termites».
fact: Names of peoples and places usually start with a capital letter.
exercise: «The Matabele live around Bulawayo in south-western Zimbabwe.» Where do the Matabele live? | In the city of London | On the coast of Australia | *Around Bulawayo in south-western Zimbabwe | In northern Scotland
exercise: «Matabele ants of Africa raid termites.» What does Matabele name in this sentence? | *A kind of ant | A type of termite | A region of Zimbabwe | A history lesson
exercise: Today the people are usually called what? | Zimbabwe | Matabele | *Ndebele | Bulawayo
test: Matabeleland means which of these? | A city in Zimbabwe | A war between two countries | *The region where the Matabele live | A kind of ant
test: Which subject would you most likely meet the word Matabele in? | Music lessons about drums | *History lessons about southern Africa | Science lessons about planets | Maths lessons about shapes
exam: Why might a history book now write Ndebele instead of Matabele? | Ndebele is a kind of ant | Ndebele is the name of a city in London | *Ndebele is what the people are usually called today | Ndebele means very old
